1
00:00:00,174 --> 00:00:03,224
The Himalayas hold more ice
than anywhere outside the poles.

2
00:00:03,449 --> 00:00:07,340
Three great rivers start there:
the Indus, Ganga and Brahmaputra.

3
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:09,730
Hundreds of millions of
people live downstream.

4
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:11,530
First, melt would flood rivers.

5
00:00:11,736 --> 00:00:15,126
Then, once the ice is gone,
the dry-season flow would drop.

6
00:00:15,241 --> 00:00:18,051
The Indus depends most
on glacier and snow melt.

7
00:00:18,062 --> 00:00:20,652
The Ganga relies more on
the monsoon and groundwater.

8
00:00:21,017 --> 00:00:22,387
The Brahmaputra is mixed.

9
00:00:22,557 --> 00:00:27,067
Ten years is far faster than scientists
expect, but the direction is real.

10
00:00:27,128 --> 00:00:29,118
Which river would you worry about most?

11
00:00:29,148 --> 00:00:29,778
Comment.

